Core Differences between YOLOv8 and YOLO11
• No difference in detection philosophy:
• both are one-stage detectors;
• both use P3/P4/P5;
• both use an FPN/PAN neck;
• both use DFL for box regression;
• both use sigmoid/BCE for classification.
• The main difference is in feature representation blocks:
• YOLOv8 uses C2f;
• YOLO11 uses C3k2;
• YOLO11 adds C2PSA after SPPF in the backbone.
Message
YOLOv8 and YOLO11 share the same “conceptual backbone” for the detection
head; YOLO11 improves how features are extracted and refined before being passed
to the head.

What to Remember After This Lecture
• Do not learn YOLO only by version names; learn it through the structure:
data →feature pyramid →head →decode →evaluation
• When reading YOLO source code:
• read the YAML file to understand the model graph;
• read block.py to understand backbone/neck blocks;
• read head.py to understand the Detect head;
• read loss/eval code to understand training and mAP computation.
• The final goal: not only to use YOLO, but to modify YOLO, analyze YOLO,
and design new detectors.
